  "question": "A network chat program is designed to implement network communication-related functions, with the following functional requirements:\n\nStore basic user information, including user ID, username, password, email, user IP address, user port number, and the time of the user's last login. This table can be used for user login verification, user information queries, etc.\n\nAdditionally, store the chat records of each user, including message ID, sender ID, receiver ID, message content, and sending time. This table can be used for historical message queries, message records, etc.\n\nFurthermore, it is necessary to store server configuration information, including server ID, server IP address, server port number, maximum client connections, receive buffer size, and the protocol used. This table can be used for server configuration management and dynamic adjustment of server parameters.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0415\nCREATE TABLE `user_info` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `user_port_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `chat_record` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `sending_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  KEY `chat_record_ibfk_1` (`sender_id`),\n  KEY `chat_record_ibfk_2` (`receiver_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `chat_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `user_info` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `chat_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `user_info` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `server_config` (\n  `server_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `server_ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `server_port_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `max_client_connections` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receive_buffer_size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `protocol` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`server_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
